  cons section portable "Portable execution CI" body
    cons paragraph
      cons "WASI foundationは[同/おな]じcomponentをWasmtime 44.0.1のnative codegenとPulley64で[実行/じっこう]し、[終了状態/しゅうりょうじょうたい]・[試験数/しけんすう]・elapsed[以外/いがい]の[出力/しゅつりょく]を[比較/ひかく]します。"
      cons "PulleyもCraneliftでbytecodeを[生成/せいせい]するため、[別/べつ]compilerの[検証/けんしょう]とは[扱/あつか]いません。"
      cons "[空/から]のlibrary test binaryはemptyとして[記録/きろく]し、[集約/しゅうやく]では[実試験/じつしけん]の[成功/せいこう]を[要求/ようきゅう]します。"
      cons "[各/かく]processは180[秒/びょう]で[停止/ていし]・[回収/かいしゅう]し、[失敗/しっぱい]ログもartifactへ[保存/ほぞん]します。"
      cons sentence cons ruby text "比較用" text "ひかくよう" cons text "componentは " cons code "cargo test --release" cons text " で" cons ruby text "最適化" text "さいてきか" cons text "します。" nil
      cons "[通常/つうじょう]のdebug WASI[試験/しけん]は[別途維持/べっといじ]します。"
      cons "[非最適化/ひさいてきか]のengine parse[全/ぜん]20[件/けん]はCIのPulleyで180[秒/びょう]を[超/こ]えたため、[試験/しけん]の[削除/さくじょ]やcoreの[資源上限変更/しげんじょうげんへんこう]ではなく、[配布時/はいふじ]にも[使/つか]う[最適化/さいてきか]コードを[比較/ひかく]します。" nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons link relative "../conformance/targets/rp2040/README.md" none text "RP2040 adapter" cons text " は" cons ruby text "別" text "べつ" cons text "workspaceのbare-metal harnessです。" nil
      cons "production core/reader/wire/engineの[依存/いぞん]を[使用/しよう]し、HAL・UART・allocatorを[外側/そとがわ]へ[置/お]きます。"
      cons "ARMv6-M buildと[固定版/こていばん]rp2040jsでのUF2[実行/じっこう]は[別/べつ]job・[別証拠/べつしょうこ]です。"
      cons "[初期実行範囲/しょきじっこうはんい]はsource[位置/いち]・budget・NDFの4[件/けん]で、Reader/Engine[全受入/ぜんうけいれ]や[実機試験/じっきしけん]の[代/か]わりにはしません。" nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "[実/じつ]ブラウザのWasm・Playground、RISC-V、big-endianの[検査/けんさ]はそれぞれ[独立/どくりつ]した[未達範囲/みたつはんい]です。"
      cons "このCI[整備/せいび]をDoc HTML・[文書移行/ぶんしょいこう]・Pages[公開/こうかい]の[完成/かんせい]へ[読/よ]み[替/か]えません。"
      cons "CIの[区切/くぎ]り[後/ご]はDoc[生成/せいせい]を[進/すす]め、[意味/いみ]・リンク・[安定/あんてい]IDの[対応/たいおう]を[検証/けんしょう]できたページからnepld[正本/せいほん]へ[移行/いこう]し、[検査済/けんさず]みの[同/おな]じsite artifactを[公開/こうかい]します。" nil
    cons section inlineSchemaFrontier "Inline schema-validation frontier" body
      cons paragraph
        cons "Structural validation retains up to eight borrowed sibling groups in a fixed inline array. "
        cons "Each group pairs a value slice with one expected type or an exactly aligned field-descriptor slice. "
        cons "A remainder reuses the slot freed by its current group; unary chains retain no empty ancestors. "
        cons "Wider lists no longer require storage proportional to their width, while deeply branching inputs spill with precharged fallible capacity sized for the actual group. "
        cons "The frontier retains overflow capacity for reuse." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "Traversal and schema checks remain forward depth-first. "
        cons "Every child is still charged individually for Work before any child Nodes/depth check, preserving partial Work usage and ordinary error order with Allocation nonbinding. "
        cons "Allocation-versus-Work stop precedence can change because the real storage requests change; larger groups may cost more for deeply branching inputs. "
        cons "Zero-allocation wide-input and exact/one-short deep-branch spill regressions cover both sides of this tradeoff. "
        cons "Removed AllocationUnits represent removed heap requests, not waived validation. "
        cons "Full acceptance remains separate." nil
      nil
    nil
  cons section savedExecutionScope "Pure saved execution-scope derivation" body
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "ExecutionScope::child" cons text " polls the shared Budget, applies the heap-free pure transition in " cons code "suspension/execution/admission.rs" cons text ", and records a typed depth stop when derivation fails. " nil
      cons "Each saved child limit is the minimum of its parent and requested limits; depth is a checked increment bounded by the resulting depth ceiling. "
      cons "Child construction does not perform callback/resource admission. "
      cons sentence cons code "ExecutionScope::run" cons text " retains that responsibility across Await." nil nil
    cons rawcode some "sh" "CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true cargo kani -p nepl3-suite --harness suspension::execution::verification::\n"
    cons paragraph
      cons "The derivation harness checks arbitrary saved/requested u64 fields against a u128 depth reference and explicit field minima, including two-step ancestor composition. "
      cons "A separate harness calls the actual public child method with arbitrary observed Usage and all prior stop reasons, checking unchanged accounting and first-stop precedence. "
      cons "That wrapper harness uses unlimited current Budget ceilings and active depth zero; it does not prove arbitrary current Budget ceilings, active depth or private measurement state. "
      cons "Native boundary tests additionally cover active host depth four, overflow, exact and one-short depth ceilings. "
      cons "Existing scheduler/root integration tests remain required. "
      cons "Neither harness establishes scheduler correctness, authorization, callback execution, whole-runtime purity or physical memory bounds. "
      cons "T11/T12 and the existing acceptance entries are not completed by this change." nil
    nil
  cons section resourceTransitions "Pure resource-transition verification" body
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::charge" cons text " applies the pure scalar transition in " cons code "budget/charge.rs" cons text ". " nil
      cons "The transition receives the prior counter, limit, amount and first stop and returns a typed charged/stopped outcome. "
      cons "Its mutable application boundary updates only the selected counter and stop. "
      cons "This is a bounded implementation scope, not a claim that every Budget operation or core API is pure." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons text "The Kani harness in " cons code "budget/verification.rs" cons text " calls that same production method. " nil
      cons "It admits all u64 fields, all seven resources and all nine current stop reasons, including overflow, zero charge, a counter above a lowered ceiling and an existing stop. "
      cons "A u128 specification checks the result and complete Usage; limits, active depth and observed depth must remain unchanged. "
      cons "The harness has no loops, recursion, input assumptions or alternate verification implementation. "
      cons "Its enum generators must be updated when resource or stop variants are added." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::observe_depth" cons text " likewise applies the pure transition in " cons code "budget/depth.rs" cons text ". " nil
      cons "Its production harness admits arbitrary active depth, relative depth, ceiling, prior stop, historical Usage depth and current measurement depth. "
      cons "It checks the u128 absolute-depth sum, first-stop precedence, both independent high-water marks and every unrelated field. "
      cons "Old marks above a lowered ceiling are retained; only the newly observed absolute depth is checked here. "
      cons sentence cons text "This individual harness does not prove " cons code "measure_depth" cons text ", " cons code "with_depth" cons text ", " cons code "with_ceiling" cons text " or callback restoration." nil nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Use Kani 0.68.0 (CBMC 6.11.0, bundled nightly-2026-08-21) separately from the normal Rust 1.97 toolchain. "
      cons "Kani is a development tool and introduces no production dependency. "
      cons "Install it following its official installation guide:" nil
    cons rawcode some "sh" "cargo install --locked kani-verifier --version 0.68.0\ncargo kani setup\ncargo fetch --locked\nCARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true cargo kani -p nepl3-core --harness budget::verification::\n"
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons text "Kani 0.68.0 does not accept " cons code "--locked" cons text ". " nil
      cons "Preserve and compare Cargo.lock before and after verification; a missing offline dependency is an execution failure, not a passed proof. "
      cons "Keep the exact source revision, lock hash, tool versions, command and raw output with the run evidence. "
      cons "Normal tests, Clippy and target builds remain separate checks. "
      cons "The harnesses cover the individual transitions and callback boundaries described here. "
      cons "They do not prove other Budget operations, schema traversal, physical memory bounds or the compiler/verifier's own correctness." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::record_observed_usage" cons text " applies " cons code "budget/observed.rs" cons text " as a pure transition of Usage, measurement depth and sticky stop. " nil
      cons "Its production Kani harness checks all eight fields together using u128 reference sums: admission is atomic, field-error precedence is preserved, and admitted already-completed work is recorded even after an existing stop. "
      cons "Failed admission retains Usage and the measurement mark; limits and active depth are unchanged. "
      cons "This proof does not authenticate host observations or establish the saved grant that authorizes them." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::with_depth" cons text " and " cons code "with_depth_at_least" cons text " share the pure entry transition in " cons code "budget/depth/entry.rs" cons text ". " nil
      cons "Two production-method harnesses check admission, first-stop precedence, independent high-water marks and callback suppression on rejection. "
      cons "A symbolic callback checks entry state and supplies an arbitrary terminating post-state and Result. "
      cons "The wrappers restore only saved active depth and preserve all other post-callback fields and the callback Result, even when that Result differs from the sticky stop. "
      cons "These proofs concern this boundary, not callback computations, generic error conversions, panic/unwind restoration, divergence or authorization to replace/reset a Budget. "
      cons "They do not establish Usage monotonicity across an arbitrary whole-Budget replacement." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons text "The required " cons code "resource-charge-proof" cons text " CI job runs the pinned verifier and keeps its raw output and source/lock identity for 14 days. " nil
      cons "The quality gate requires this job to succeed; the artifact is scoped proof evidence, not full acceptance." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::with_ceiling" cons text " uses the pure admission function " cons code "budget/ceiling.rs" cons text ". " nil
      cons "The eight effective limits are component-wise minima. "
      cons "Admission checks cumulative usage in source/work/nodes/allocation/output/diagnostics/events order, then checks historical usage depth last; active and measurement depth are not admission inputs. "
      cons "The production-method Kani harness uses arbitrary fields and prior stops, checks callback suppression on rejection and entry state on admission, and models an arbitrary replacement Budget with an independent callback Result. "
      cons "Every returning path restores only the saved outer limits; other callback state and its Result are retained. "
      cons "Nested ceiling intersection cannot widen limits, but a callback that directly replaces its Budget is not constrained by that guarantee. "
      cons "Panic, unwind, divergence, generic error conversion and whole-runtime acceptance remain outside this proof." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons code "Budget::measure_depth" cons text " completes its local observation through the pure " cons code "budget/depth/measurement.rs" cons text " function. " nil
      cons "Entry rejects a prior stop before the callback; otherwise the local mark starts at the caller's active depth. "
      cons "Every returning callback path merges the local mark into the saved enclosing mark before resolving the Result. "
      cons "A callback error takes precedence over a different sticky stop. "
      cons "A successful callback is followed by a stop check and returns the nonnegative difference from the saved base only when still running. "
      cons "The production-method Kani harness checks these rules, entry state, callback count and unchanged post-callback fields using arbitrary symbolic states. "
      cons "Its signed wider-integer difference is independent of production saturating_sub. "
      cons "The arbitrary post-state model probes the wrapper boundary and does not authorize Budget replacement: the public contract remains limited to pure validation callbacks that never replace the Budget. "
      cons "Ordinary nested tests also check a semantic validation error concurrent with resource exhaustion. "
      cons "This does not prove validation internals, generic error conversions, panic/unwind, divergence, or formal acceptance." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "Shape admission callers must also preserve depth overflow before calling Budget. "
      cons "The Math, Doc and Sentence graph validators use checked addition for caller base plus the live traversal stack and cached subtree height. "
      cons "Saturating these sums would hide an overflowing depth when the configured limit itself is u64::MAX. "
      cons sentence cons text "Their " cons code "--test shape absolute_depth_overflow" cons text " regressions cover one-node shapes and shared DAGs at exact-fit and overflowing bases, restored active depth, retained charges and a sticky DepthLimit. " nil
      cons "The DAG fixtures visit the shared child first on a shorter path, so the longest-path check cannot be replaced by the maximum live stack. "
      cons "This is a caller-side regression scope, not a proof of every rendering, lowering, evaluation or host depth calculation." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons "The same overflow gate applies when a previously checked handle is reused at a higher caller depth: Math binding analysis and evaluation, Sentence plain-text rendering, foreign occurrence enumeration and foreign closure validation reject an overflowing absolute depth with sticky DepthLimit. "
      cons "These callers retain their existing charge order and restore the enclosing active depth through Budget. "
      cons "Regressions create each handle at base zero using the same Budget before testing the higher base. "
      cons "One-node exact-fit controls cover binding, evaluation, text and shape-only foreign enumeration; the foreign validation regression instead checks that overflow is rejected before an intentionally invalid guest is validated. "
      cons "These examples do not prove guest execution or all host-side depth calculations." nil
    cons paragraph
      cons sentence cons text "A host-side Reader composition regression in " cons code "nepl3-provider --test reader" cons text " carries the saved terminal Read proof through Connection::send, fragmented Connection::receive_pending_reply, source admission, typed Report comparison and ReaderSession::resume. " nil
      cons "A source-policy failure closes the transport and preserves the Reader slot; subsequent send/receive attempts perform no I/O. "
      cons "A truncated Reader frame also preserves the slot. "
      cons "A later domain Report mismatch leaves the slot pending but does not retroactively close the successfully admitted transport. "
      cons "The successful path preserves the Unicode diagnostic/mapping and consumes exactly one frame before a following Close. "
      cons "Only resume consumes the Reader slot. "
      cons "The Reader dependency is test-only. "
      cons "This is same-process I/O composition using a shared cumulative Budget, not a remote Reader implementation or authenticated cross-process usage accounting." nil
    cons section sourceAdmissionInterruption "Source admission interruption coverage" body
      cons paragraph
        cons sentence cons code "cargo test --locked -p nepl3-core --lib source::tests::" cons text " exercises actual " cons code "SourceAdmission::admit_existing" cons text " calls using fixed valid UTF-8 snapshots. " nil
        cons "It sweeps each SourceBytes, Work and AllocationUnits ceiling from zero through an ample-budget baseline call's usage, checks all nine prior stop reasons, and preserves the first stop on a direct retry. "
        cons "The two-entry seed covers a fresh middle key, independently stored duplicates, shared-storage duplicates, digest conflicts and locator conflicts. "
        cons "Assertions check the admission order, sorted index, shared-storage membership/order, retained earlier entries and unchanged counters unrelated to admission. "
        cons "A late allocation-stop witness checks that an already charged SourceBytes amount is retained without publishing a partial ledger. "
        cons "The empty-ledger case has its own baseline-derived ceiling sweep. "
        cons "Fixture hashes and locators are checked independently by a normal test." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "This is native boundary-test evidence, not formal verification. "
        cons "Experimental Kani 0.68.0 checks of both the two-entry ledger and the reduced first-admission case reported out-of-memory failures; neither established a proof. "
        cons "Their experimental checkpoint is kept separately and no unverified harness is added to the CI proof gate. "
        cons "The tests do not establish arbitrary ledger/text bounds, exact Work/Allocation costs, physical allocation failure handling, remote usage authentication or complete runtime acceptance. "
        cons "The existing scoped resource proofs and the outstanding acceptance states are unchanged." nil
      nil
    cons section savedScopeReentry "Saved execution-scope re-entry coverage" body
      cons paragraph
        cons sentence cons text "The suite's " cons code "suspension::execution::tests::" cons text " native regressions cover the actual " cons code "ExecutionScope::root" cons text " and " cons code "run" cons text " composition. " nil
        cons "A saved frame whose Work ceiling has already been exceeded is rejected before observing its saved depth: the callback is suppressed and the full Usage value is unchanged. "
        cons "This distinguishes the required ceiling-before-depth wrapper order from the reversed order, even though each Budget wrapper has separate scoped proofs. "
        cons "A later zero-depth ceiling also rejects a saved frame without callback execution or a new depth observation. "
        cons "Further cases retain a temporary capture ceiling after the outer ceiling is restored, and preserve a typed callback error and charged work while restoring outer limits and a nonzero active host depth. "
        cons sentence cons text "Root construction intentionally defers cumulative resource admission until " cons code "run" cons text "." nil nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "These are native composition regressions, not additional formal proofs or a claim that a production defect was found. "
        cons "They do not establish scheduler or remote-host correctness, panic/unwind restoration, or complete runtime acceptance." nil
      nil
    cons section markdownBatchReuse "Markdown batch validation reuse" body
      cons paragraph
        cons "The annotated Math preparation loop validates its immutable containing Doc once when it encounters the first Math node. "
        cons sentence cons text "Crate-private host helpers reuse that native " cons code "ValidatedDocumentSyntax" cons text " only inside the same registry, source-admission ledger, cumulative Budget and active-depth scope. " nil
        cons "Each selected Math guest still passes the existing schema/foreign-closure validation, lowering, shape checking, MathML and structural TeX preparation. "
        cons "Public single-node entry points continue validating arbitrary input. "
        cons "This is not a portable or cross-operation paid-work proof. "
        cons "Full Doc validation still includes unselected nodes and embeds. "
        cons "The loop rejects changed limits or active depth before reuse and after every guest preparation, including the last guest. "
        cons "This guard does not detect an arbitrary custom codec replacing the Budget with another value having identical bounds; preserving cumulative usage remains the codec's contract." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "The SVG page profile prepares plain text lazily at the first image requirement and reuses it for that page's later images. "
        cons "Image-free pages retain complete PageSet admission without redundant alt-text preparation. "
        cons "Static SVG validation, asset resolution and rejection of unused assets remain in place. "
        cons "All phases use the original cumulative Budget; stops are not reset and limits are not raised. "
        cons "Math preparation now precedes lazy image preparation, so competing failures can be reported in a different order; byte-identical error strings are not promised." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "Regression coverage compares multiple Math fragments with the independently validating public path and requires lower Work and AllocationUnits. "
        cons "Image-free pages must match the plain page profile's complete Usage and output. "
        cons "Multi-Math page cases retain exact/one-below limits, cancellation, elevated caller depth, invalid origin/unreachable node/unused embed rejection, and faithful output. "
        cons "These native checks do not complete formal acceptance or prove all rendering paths linear-time." nil
      nil
    cons section checkedPagesetReuse "Checked PageSet preparation reuse" body
      cons paragraph
        cons "PageSet resolution hashes the enclosing PageSet and document values together. "
        cons "Guest identities now use versioned Foundation components and operation-domain wrapping; group NDF reuse across that encoding boundary remains unfinished. "
        cons "It keeps all native closure, source, environment and outer schema checks, and preserves independently separated digest domains. "
        cons "Standalone preparation still encodes/checks its input. "
        cons "Guest hash work now precedes label discovery, so competing failure order may change. "
        cons "Tests compare mixed empty/single/multiple guest pages with independent standalone component identities and exact/one-short resource ceilings." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "The same operation retains immutable native document structures in CheckedPages. "
        cons "Selected Markdown Math preparation borrows these structures instead of repeating containing-Doc validation; guest selection, semantic checks, lowering and output preparation remain. "
        cons "The native unresolved-text entry shares the ordinary text traversal, but accepts no external resolutions and therefore needs no identity hashes for their verification. "
        cons "Encountered inline guests remain unresolved. "
        cons "This supplies image alt text without re-encoding and re-hashing its full owner." nil
      cons paragraph
        cons "Both native entries check limits and active depth, preserve stopped budgets, and require continuation of the same cumulative Budget/registry/source admission. "
        cons "Matching bounds do not prove paid-usage identity. "
        cons "These are in-operation native proofs, not wire receipts, cache authorization, guest semantic proofs or complete runtime acceptance. "
        cons "No resource ceiling is raised or reset." nil
      nil
    cons section digestRequestLookup "Digest request lookup probes" body
      cons paragraph
        cons "A batch node visit finds the first matching immutable-reference request with one charged lower-bound search, then scans equal requests in their existing order. "
        cons "Every run candidate and one terminal probe are charged, including end-of-index; completed requests consume the probe but do not restart hashes. "
        cons "This replaces a second binary search without tying Usage to address rank. "
        cons "The domain, encoding, active hash scopes, insertion shifts and request-order results are unchanged. "
        cons "Direct regressions cover missing addresses and duplicate runs at different ranks, all short Work ceilings, sticky stops and completed matches. "
        cons "No universal CPU speedup is claimed for duplicate-heavy inputs; the deterministic Work change and actual encoding/hash outputs are separate measurements." nil
      nil
